  "description": "A split-level home on a cul-de-sac in Ewing, set on a third of an acre backing to woods with direct access to the Delaware & Raritan Canal towpath. The foyer opens into living space with refinished hardwood, Andersen replacement windows, recessed lighting and crown molding. A large bay window fills the living room, which flows into the formal dining room. The updated eat-in kitchen has stainless double ovens, a cooktop, a custom tile backsplash, abundant cabinetry and generous counter space. The family room sits at the heart of the plan and opens directly onto a screened porch overlooking the wooded rear yard. A first-floor bedroom works as a guest room, home office or playroom, with three more bedrooms and two updated full bathrooms upstairs. Baseboard hot-water heat on natural gas, central air, well water and public sewer. Minutes from TCNJ, Rider University, Capital Health Medical Center, Mercer County Airport, NJ Transit and I-295.",
